    <body n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0487.pyrphoros.meineke1841-grc1" xml:lang="grc">
      <div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0487.pyrphoros.meineke1841-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0487_pyrphoros">
        <head>ΠΥΡΦΟΡΟΣ</head>
        <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="unnumbered" ana="#compiled-unnumbered-fragment" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered">
          <lg>
            <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l1">Οὐκ ἔστιν οὔτε ζωγράφος, μὰ τοὺς θεούς,</l>
            <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l2">οὔτ᾽ ἀνδριαντοποιός, ὅστις ἂν πλάσαι</l>
            <l n="3" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l3">κάλλος τοιοῦτον, οἷον ἡ ἀλήθει᾽ ἔχει.</l>
            <l n="4" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l4">οὔτ᾽ ἀνδριάντος γὰρ καλῶς πεπλασμένου,</l>
            <l n="5" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l5">ἂν μὴ τὸν αἰσθησόμενον ἡ τέχνη λάβῃ.</l>
          </lg>
          <note type="apparatus">
            <bibl>Stobaeus Flor. LXV 5</bibl>. Vs. 1 <quote>μετὰ</quote> pro <quote>μὰ</quote> cod. A. — Vs. 2 <quote>ὅστις</quote> A et Grotius. Vulgo <quote>τις</quote>. — Vs. 3 <quote>τοσοῦτον</quote> A. — Vs. 4 possis <quote>οὐδ᾽ ἀνδριάντες γὰρ καλῶς πεπλασμένοι</quote>. Sed nec hoc sufficit. Excidisse versum, cuius haec fere fuerit sententia: <quote>οὔτ᾽ ὄφελος οὐδὲν εὖ γεγραμμένης γραφῆς</quote>, coniicit Porsonus Misc. p. 255.</note>
          <quote>
            <lg>
              <l n="1_2" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l1_2">Edepol nec pictor quisquam est nec statuarius,</l>
              <l n="2_2" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l2_2">qui talem possit arte pulchritudinem</l>
              <l n="3_2" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l3_2">exprimere qualem rerum veritas habet.</l>
              <l n="4_2" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l4_2">at vero periit usus simulachrûm omnium,</l>
              <l n="5_2" xml:id="meineke-0487-pyrphoros-unnumbered-l5_2">nisi ars peritos iudices invenerit.</l>
            </lg>
          </quote>
        </div>
      </div>
